  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A rock is thrown vertically upwards with an initial speed of 40 m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span> from point A on the surface of planet X. The planet has no atmosphere. The diagram shows four photos of the rock taken at 2 second intervals. At point B, the rock is moving upwards with a speed of 16 m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span> .</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>What is the best estimate for the acceleration of free fall on planet X?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">3 m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span> </li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">4 m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span> </li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">7 m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span> </li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">9 m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span> </li>\n</ol>"
  },
